# Firebase / Google service-account keys — NEVER commit.
# These carry a private_key granting admin access to the Firebase project.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*-service-account*.json
service-account*.json
# Store-listing / marketing assets: 40.7 MB of screenshots, iPad captures and a
# 13 MB zip. None of it enters the app binary, but EAS builds its upload archive
# from git-tracked files, so tracking them meant re-uploading 40 MB on EVERY
# build — a ~39 minute upload on a slow link, and the cause of repeated
# `write ECONNRESET` failures. Untracked in this commit; the files remain on
# disk and in git history, so nothing is lost.
store-assets/

# Google Play service-account credentials — NEVER commit
play-service-account.json
# Written by `eas credentials`; holds the Android keystore password,
# key alias and key password in PLAINTEXT. Never commit.
credentials.json
credentials/
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
